course: dictionary
lesson: 14340
title: Words for things that happen
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: An occurrence is something that happens. You can think of it as an event, a thing that takes place. «The sudden power cut was a strange occurrence in our street.» The sentence tells you something happened, and the word strange tells you how it felt.
explain: Occurrence can also mean how often something happens. «The occurrence of storms in winter is high in our town.» Here the word is about a pattern, so it means how often storms happen, not just one storm.
explain: Look for clues like common and rare. «Late buses are a common occurrence» means they happen often. «A snowfall in July is a rare occurrence» means it hardly ever happens. The clue word tells you how often.
fact: An occurrence is something that happens, an event.
fact: «Occurrence» can mean how often something happens, as in the occurrence of storms.
fact: A common occurrence happens often, and a rare occurrence hardly ever happens.
fact: In formal writing, occurrence can mean being found somewhere, as in the occurrence of gold in rocks.
fact: In maths, you can count the occurrence of each number in a list.
exercise: «The lightning flash was a rare occurrence in our town.» What does rare occurrence mean? | Something that happens every day | A kind of cloud | A loud noise from a shop | *Something that hardly ever happens
exercise: In maths, Priya counts the occurrence of the number 7 in a list. What is she counting? | *The number of times 7 appears | The size of the list | The colour of the paper | The shape of the number 7
exercise: «The occurrence of gold in these rocks surprised the scientists.» What does occurrence mean here? | Being cut into pieces | Being sold in a shop | Being lost forever | *Being found somewhere
test: «Late buses are a common occurrence in our town.» What does common occurrence mean? | *Something that happens often | Something that happens once a year | Something that never happens | Something that is a secret
test: Ben says a thunderstorm is an occurrence. What does he mean? | A type of cloud | A game we play at school | A loud noise only | *It is something that happens
exam: «The occurrence of storms in winter is high, so storms happen a lot.» In this sentence, what does occurrence mean? | The name of a storm | *How often storms happen | A storm that is over | A map of the weather
